{title: 455 - Immortal Love, Forever Full}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #455 • SERENITY • 8.6.9.6}
{lyricist: John Greenleaf Whittier}
{composer: William V. Wallace}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 455}
{meta: tune SERENITY}
{meta: meter 8.6.9.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/A]Immortal [A7]Love, forever [C#m/G#]full,
[A7/G]Forever flowing [D/A]free,
[A7/G]Forever shared, [A#m]forever [F#m]whole,
[D/F#]A never ebbing sea!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/A]We nay not [A7]climb the [G#7]heavenly [C#m/G#]steeps
[A7/G]To bring the Lord Christ [D/A]down;
[A7/G]In vain we [A#m]search [Bm]the [Em]lowest [A7/G]deeps,
[D/F#]For him no depths can drown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/A]But warm, so [A7]tender, [G#7]even [C#m/G#]yet
[A7/G]A present help is [D/A]He;
[A7/G]And faith has [A#m]still [Bm]its [Em]Olivet,
[D/F#]And love its Galilee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/A]The healing [A7]of His [G#7]seamless [C#m/G#]dress
[A7/G]Is by our beds of [D/A]pain;
[A7/G]We touch Him in [A#m]life's [F#m]throng and [A7/G]press,
[D/F#]And we are whole again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D/A]Through Him the [A7]first fond [G#7]prayers are [C#m/G#]said,
[A7/G]Our lips of childhood [D/A]frame;
[A7/G]The last low [A#m]whispers [Em]of [F#m]our [A7/G]dead
[D/F#]Are burdened with His name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D/A]O Lord and [A7]Master [G#7]of us [C#m/G#]all:
[A7/G]Whate'er our names or [D/A]sign,
[A7/G]We own Thy [A#m]sway, [Bm]we [Em]hear [F#m]Thy [A7/G]call,
[D/F#]We test our lives by Thine!
{end_of_verse}
